---
title: CLI
order: 2
---

The Barque CLI lets you initialize Barque locally, capture project content, and search across captures.

## Install

Install the `barque` cli from NPM.

```bash
bun install @barque/cli
```

## Quick start

```bash
# Start Barque locally and configure your agent
barque init

# List your projects
barque projects

# Capture a note into a project
barque capture --project my-project --text "Ships on Friday"

# Search captures in a project
barque search --project my-project --query "Ships"
```

## Commands

### `barque init`

Initializes Barque in the current directory.

- Verifies Docker is running and starts the Barque server on `http://localhost:8193` if needed.
- Prompts for your coding agent and writes a `barque` skill file into the matching agent config directory.
- Stores the selected agent in `~/.config/barque/credentials.json`.

### `barque projects`

Lists projects you own.

```bash
barque projects
barque p
```

### `barque capture`

Captures content for a project. Exactly one capture mode is required.

```bash
# Capture text
barque capture --project my-project --text "Release checklist"

# Capture a URL
barque capture --project my-project --url "https://example.com/roadmap"

# Capture JSON data
barque capture --project my-project --data '{"title":"Spec","version":3}'
```

Options:

- `--project`, `-p` (required): project name to capture into
- `--text`, `-t`: raw text content
- `--url`, `-u`: URL to fetch and capture
- `--data`, `-d`: JSON string payload

### `barque search`

Searches captured content within a project.

```bash
barque search --project my-project --query "roadmap"
barque s -p my-project -q "roadmap"
```

Options:

- `--project`, `-p`: project id to search within
- `--query`, `-q` (required): search query

### `barque logs`

Prints the CLI command history log.

```bash
barque logs
barque lg
```

Logs are stored under `.barque/history.log` in the directory where you ran the command. The file rotates when it grows past 10MB.
